@@ -108,9 +107,19 @@ All IPC communication uses named channels defined in `src/shared/types.ts`:
 
 `QaService` persists every exchange to `qa-history.json` with an `id`,
 `askedAt` timestamp and optional `followUpOf` link. `getConversation()`
-normalizes it (including older entries without those fields) into
-`ConversationExchange[]`; the renderer only displays it. Follow-up questions
-add the parent question to the retrieval context in the service.
+normalizes it entry by entry (including older entries without those fields)
+into `ConversationExchange[]`; the renderer only displays it.
+
+- Malformed entries (no question or no answer) are skipped with a WARN log and
+  left in the file. A file that is not valid JSON or not a list raises a
+  user-facing "history file is unreadable (<path>)" error and is never
+  overwritten. Write failures are translated the same way.
+- Follow-up questions add the questions of the whole ancestor chain (up to 5
+  turns) to the retrieval context; retrieval ignores punctuation and stop words.
+- `clearHistory()` bumps a generation counter: an answer to a question that was
+  pending during a clear is returned but not saved. The renderer also ignores it.
+- Citation excerpts are stored as plain one-line text (`src/shared/text.ts`,
+  shared by services and renderer).
 
 ## Architecture Verification
 
